📚 Program 16 — Object-Oriented Library Record Application

📌 Description

This program demonstrates a simple object-oriented library record application using file storage.

It uses a class to represent library books and provides operations for storing and managing book information in a text file. The program combines OOP concepts with C++ file handling.

🔑 Concepts Covered

- 📚 Library book records
- 🏗️ Classes and objects
- 💾 File-based storage
- ➕ Adding book records
- 📖 Reading stored records
- 🧩 Converting objects to file records
- 🖥️ Menu-driven programming

📁 File Created

"library_books.txt"

🧠 Main Concept

Combining Object-Oriented Programming with File Streams
